From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:16:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: virtio: start a substream afresh after a system suspend

A system suspend resets the device, which drops every substream's
parameters and queued I/O messages, and the ALSA core then prepares each
substream again from the start of its buffer: it resets hw_ptr and
appl_ptr after ops->prepare(), and the driver resets its indirect PCM
state. Two pieces of state from before the suspend survived.

The suspended branch of virtsnd_pcm_prepare() kept vss->hw_ptr, the
buffer position where the substream had stopped. The first pointer call
after the restart counted that position as played, so the core position
jumped ahead and the indirect state took the queued periods for that
much less than they were. The transfer then wrote into periods still
queued, which complete with more than one period's length: from then on
each completion moved the position by two or three periods. A playback
stream suspended one period into its buffer played at twice its rate
(7/3 and 3 times two and three periods in), the data written into the
queued periods never reached the device, and the device itself kept
completing one period of real time after another. The fast phase lasted
until two completions reached one pointer call, whose modulo-buffer
count then lost a buffer and left the stream with fewer periods queued.
Restart hw_ptr in both branches.

Only a substream the core was running is suspended through the trigger.
A paused one kept vss->suspended clear and its pending message count:
its next prepare failed with -EBADFD, and an open sent PCM_RELEASE for
the messages the reset had dropped, which the reset stream refuses, so
the device could not be opened again. When the device is frozen, count
no message as pending and mark every substream for reconfiguration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/virtio/virtio_card.c    | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 sound/virtio/virtio_pcm.h     |  5 +++--
 sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_ops.c |  9 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/virtio/virtio_card.c b/sound/virtio/virtio_card.c
index a3e69a460b85faf09447b5343d9e9c137cadac21..6a8b259c86ccdbc15e5052783ad98ace46c7de48 100644
--- a/sound/virtio/virtio_card.c
+++ b/sound/virtio/virtio_card.c
@@ -387,8 +387,21 @@ static int virtsnd_freeze(struct virtio_device *vdev)
 	virtio_reset_device(vdev);
 	vdev->config->del_vqs(vdev);
 
-	for (i = 0; i < snd->nsubstreams; ++i)
-		cancel_work_sync(&snd->substreams[i].elapsed_period);
+	for (i = 0; i < snd->nsubstreams; ++i) {
+		struct virtio_pcm_substream *vss = &snd->substreams[i];
+
+		cancel_work_sync(&vss->elapsed_period);
+		/*
+		 * The reset took the parameters and the queued I/O messages of
+		 * every substream, not only of the running ones that the ALSA
+		 * core suspended: no message is pending any more, and a paused
+		 * or prepared substream must be reconfigured at its next
+		 * prepare as well.
+		 */
+		scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &vss->lock)
+			vss->msg_count = 0;
+		vss->suspended = true;
+	}
 
 	kfree(snd->event_msgs);
 	snd->event_msgs = NULL;
diff --git a/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm.h b/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm.h
index 0f3a433175e49a27e50ab8897329b765406a3958..01e7b055b217ce5aca54a7aeb9e83b86d63f4fa6 100644
--- a/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm.h
+++ b/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm.h
@@ -33,8 +33,9 @@ struct virtio_pcm_msg;
  * @xfer_xrun: Data underflow/overflow state (0 - no xrun, 1 - xrun).
  * @stopped: True if the substream is stopped and must be released on the device
  *           side.
- * @suspended: True if the substream is suspended and must be reconfigured on
- *             the device side at resume.
+ * @suspended: True if the device was reset by a system suspend since the
+ *             substream was last prepared, so that the substream must be
+ *             reconfigured on the device side at its next prepare.
  * @msgs: Allocated I/O messages.
  * @nmsgs: Number of allocated I/O messages.
  * @msg_last_enqueued: Index of the last I/O message added to the virtqueue.
diff --git a/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_ops.c b/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_ops.c
index 1091100a4c982b90e6a682e8a6e2548217b1012a..c910004efa4a45eb327b6225afdca2bbfe8e1910 100644
--- a/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_ops.c
+++ b/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_ops.c
@@ -282,7 +282,6 @@ static int virtsnd_pcm_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 		}
 
 		vss->buffer_bytes = snd_pcm_lib_buffer_bytes(substream);
-		vss->hw_ptr = 0;
 	} else {
 		struct snd_pcm_runtime *runtime = substream->runtime;
 		unsigned int buffer_bytes = snd_pcm_lib_buffer_bytes(substream);
@@ -296,6 +295,14 @@ static int virtsnd_pcm_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 			return rc;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The ALSA core restarts the substream at the beginning of the buffer
+	 * after a prepare, and so does the indirect PCM state below. The
+	 * position of the first I/O message must restart there too, also on
+	 * resume: the position the substream had when it was suspended points
+	 * into the middle of the restarted buffer.
+	 */
+	vss->hw_ptr = 0;
 	vss->xfer_xrun = false;
 	vss->suspended = false;
 	vss->msg_count = 0;
